{
  "info": {
    "name": "Modernizing Enterprise Applications — Behavior-Equivalence Suite",
    "_postman_id": "mea-equivalence-suite",
    "description": "The behavior-equivalence suite (r02-plan S6, notification-plan S2, build-plan.md §G/§D). Captured against the running Spring Boot monolith (examples/00-monolith). This collection is the project's equivalence gate: it is re-run UNCHANGED against each extracted service (starting with the Quarkus Review service, ch.15) and a service is only considered 'done' once it passes this same suite with no edits (build-plan.md §G load-bearing rule). Every request targets {{baseUrl}} so the identical collection can point at the monolith or at an extracted service's own port. Covers: (1) happy-path checkout, (2) out-of-stock, (3) payment-declined (asserting inventory is NOT left decremented, per the monolith's actual rollback behavior), (4) the Review context contract (list, get-by-id, unauthenticated POST -> 401, authenticated POST -> 201, validation -> 400) — the first extraction's externally-observable surface — and (5) the Notification context contract (DRQ-037): a checkout followed by a BOUNDED-WAIT poll of GET /api/notifications?customerId= so the identical assertion is correct whether the order-confirmation notification is written synchronously in-transaction (today's monolith, hits on the first attempt) or eventually via outbox -> Kafka -> consumer (the future async notification service, ch.17).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Smoke",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Service is reachable",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/inventory",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "inventory"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Inventory list returns 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Content-Type is application/json', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Seed inventory includes SKU-WIDGET-001 and SKU-GIZMO-003', function () {",
